# Next.js loads this automatically during `next build` (and only then — it
# does not apply to `npm run dev`), overriding the same keys in `.env`.
# See docs/hossted-env-build-vars.md for why this file exists.
#
# This file is per deployment, not a single shared value: each separate
# instance of this codebase (Hossted's own, or a client's own copy) points
# at its own backend and its own Hossted dashboard, so whoever builds THIS
# copy fills in THIS copy's own values below — there is no single correct
# "production" value to inherit from anywhere else.
#
# Only put vars here that next.config.js inlines into the browser bundle at
# build time (see its `env` key) — a server-side-only var like
# HOSSTED_UPSTREAM_TOKEN (a real secret) belongs in the Deployment/Helm
# runtime environment instead, never in a file the Docker build reads.

# This deployment's own Hossted dashboard URL (builds the "Continue with
# Hossted" link). Leave empty to disable that link.
HOSSTED_DASHBOARD_URL=

# This deployment's own proxy route — normally just this app's own
# /api/hossted at its own origin (see app/api/hossted/route.ts).
HOSSTED_PROXY_URL=
